{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:198b5833d4e9db844cd6c14c8de3c0e0aacfa18f049ce0a3e1f8f7986096a57a","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Uniform-computation-of-the-squared-logarithmic-k-server-bound-September-24-2026#thm:main","title":"thm:main"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/40358c89f8ad78314f734a68.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","generation_id":"sha256:c701139844a2d825c371ded7486924e7dae7de0af77a69dc9c1abaf1129191a1","id":"r:Uniform-computation-of-the-squared-logarithmic-k-server-bound-September-24-2026:thm:main","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Uniform-computation-of-the-squared-logarithmic-k-server-bound-September-24-2026","name":"thm:main","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":"1.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","binding":{"file":"build/source/sections/01-introduction.tex","label":"thm:main","line":21,"manuscript":"Uniform-computation-of-the-squared-logarithmic-k-server-bound-September-24-2026","statement_sha256":"73bef5c477fba6313005917b5df519c8830b3a8e072b5e3d45004d23051def9f"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Uniform-computation-of-the-squared-logarithmic-k-server-bound-September-24-2026.html#thm:main","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:a16a6eb05ae5c256675b643f6f0eba32976b72d5b9d497d710feb85aae64f8b6","file":"preprints/Uniform-computation-of-the-squared-logarithmic-k-server-bound-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":21,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"73bef5c477fba6313005917b5df519c8830b3a8e072b5e3d45004d23051def9f","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Uniform-computation-of-the-squared-logarithmic-k-server-bound-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a16a6eb05ae5c256675b643f6f0eba32976b72d5b9d497d710feb85aae64f8b6","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Uniform-computation-of-the-squared-logarithmic-k-server-bound-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/01-introduction.tex#L21"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere are an absolute constant \\(C\\) and a polynomial \\(p\\) with the following\nproperty. Let \\(n\\ge3\\), \\(2\\le k<n\\), let \\(d\\) be a rational metric on\n\\(X=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}\\), and let \\(s\\in X^k\\) be an initial labeled tuple,\nwith repetitions allowed. Write \\(L\\) for the total binary encoding length\nof \\(n,k,d,s\\). A single uniform randomized online algorithm preprocesses\nthese data in at most \\(p(L)\\) bit operations and serves request \\(r_t\\),\nfor every reachable history and internal state, in at most\n\\[\n p\\!\\left(L+\\left\\lceil\\log_2(t+1)\\right\\rceil\\right)\n\\]\nadditional bit operations. It uses only unbiased random bits and moves\nexactly one chosen server to each request, permitting a zero-length move.\nFor every fixed finite request sequence \\(\\sigma\\) independent of those bits,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main-bound}\n \\E\\cost_{A,s}(\\sigma)\n \\le C\\bigl(\\log(k+1)\\bigr)^2\\OPT_s(\\sigma)+B_{d,k,s},\n\\end{equation}\nwhere \\(B_{d,k,s}\\) is finite and independent of \\(\\sigma\\) and its length.\nThe algorithm does not need to know that length in advance."}
